      "excerpt": "The basis is indexed by all partitions; node operators add and remove cells; cell residue is c-r mod e and m_i counts cells of residue i. The facts identify addable and removable corner cells.",
      "kind": "missing-residue-labelled-partition-diagram",
      "classification": "uncertain-editorial",
      "rationale": "A small Young diagram carrying row and column indices, cell residues, and marked addable/removable corners would present the central combinatorial data of this Fock-space definition at a glance. This is a high-likelihood aid because residues and node operators are the actual indexing/action conventions used throughout, rather than a peripheral illustration.",
      "labels_and_relations_to_draw_or_check": "Draw a finite partition Young diagram with rows and columns explicitly indexed from 1. Label each cell by c-r mod e (or illustrate a concrete e such as e=3 with the residue convention in the caption), mark example addable and removable corners by their residues, and identify m_i as the count of i-residue cells. Do not imply only e-regular partitions occur: the defined Fock basis includes all partitions.",
